# BitmapTexturePool: bound GPU texture memory, plus the A/B knobs for it.
# Merged from: webkit-texpool-compositor-sync-env, webkit-texpool-synchronous-cap.
#
# The pool's unused-texture release runs on a WebProcess main-thread timer that
# starves exactly when texture churn peaks (video playback, page load), so
# released frame/tile textures accumulate without bound — device-measured 1.27 GB
# of dead 1080p video-frame textures in one WebProcess, i.e. phone swap-thrash
# and OOM. The cap is therefore enforced synchronously in acquireTexture() on the
# compositor thread (GL context guaranteed current), scoped to free
# (refCount == 1) entries.
#
# Flags:
#   WEBKIT_TEXTURE_POOL_CAP_MB       pool cap; 0 = stock (A/B)
#   WEBKIT_TEXPOOL_LOG=1             pool stats
#   WEBKIT_BITMAP_TEXTURE_POOL_DISABLED=1   bypass the pool entirely (diagnostic)
#   WEBKIT_COMPOSITOR_GL_FINISH=1    glFinish per composite (diagnostic)
#
# ---
